### Distributed Job Scheduler — sample requests (VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# Set apiKey to one of the values in API_KEYS (.env). Request names let later requests reuse
# ids from earlier responses, e.g. {{submit.response.body.id}}.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiKey = change-me-api-key

### Submit a job (201 Created)
# @name submit
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "payload": "hello", "priority": 1 }

### Get the job just submitted
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{submit.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Submit a job that always fails (ends DEAD after 3 attempts)
# @name failing
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "payload": "fail", "priority": 5, "maxAttempts": 3 }

### Slow job with a short timeout (times out, retried, then DEAD)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "payload": "delayMs=10000", "timeoutSeconds": 2, "maxAttempts": 2 }

### Delayed job: run in 60 seconds (status SCHEDULED)
# @name delayed
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "payload": "later", "delaySeconds": 60 }

### Delayed job at an absolute time (ISO-8601)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "payload": "at a time", "runAt": "2030-01-01T09:00:00Z" }

### Idempotent submit: send twice -> 201 then 200 with the same job
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: order-{{$randomInt 1 1000000}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "payload": "charge customer" }

### Cancel the delayed job (200, CANCELLED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{delayed.response.body.id}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### List jobs: paginated, filterable (status may repeat)
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs?status=DEAD&status=SUCCEEDED&type=EMAIL&page=0&size=20
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### List jobs created in a time window
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs?createdFrom=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z&createdTo=2030-01-01T00:00:00Z
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Dead-letter jobs
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/dead
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Requeue a DEAD job (run after the failing job is DEAD)
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs/{{failing.response.body.id}}/requeue
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Counts by status and successes by worker
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/stats
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ schedules

### Create a recurring schedule (5- or 6-field cron, or @hourly/@daily/...)
# @name schedule
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{
  "name": "heartbeat-email-{{$randomInt 1 1000000}}",
  "cron": "*/1 * * * *",
  "timezone": "UTC",
  "type": "EMAIL",
  "payload": "scheduled run",
  "priority": 3
}

### List schedules
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedules?page=0&size=20
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Get one schedule
GET {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{schedule.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Change the cron expression (partial update)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{schedule.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "cron": "0 */5 * * * *", "timezone": "Asia/Kolkata" }

### Pause
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{schedule.response.body.id}}/pause
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Resume (next run is computed from now; missed runs are skipped)
POST {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{schedule.response.body.id}}/resume
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Delete (existing job runs are kept)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/schedules/{{schedule.response.body.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------ errors

### Missing API key -> 401 problem+json
GET {{baseUrl}}/jobs/stats

### Validation error -> 400 problem+json
POST {{baseUrl}}/jobs
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

{ "type": "EMAIL", "priority": 42 }
